    {
      "id": "CUD-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-compact-unfolding-jacobian",
      "title": "The reciprocal real Jacobian in compact unfolding",
      "statement": "For W in the archimedean special linear group, K₁={A_(s⁻¹)p:s∈W,p∈K} has K⊆A_sK₁. If |detℝ A_s|≤D₀ on W then ∫_(K₁)f(A_sp) dμ≥D₀⁻¹∫_K f dμ for each s∈W. At one place |detℝ A_g|=|detℂ g|^(−2N), so D₀=1 is admissible for the determinant-one group.",
      "hypotheses": "N≥1, K compact in the positive cone, W the closed entrywise ball of radius 1/2 around the identity in the finite product of special linear groups. μ additive Haar measure, f nonnegative measurable, and A_g inverse congruence.",
      "correspondence": "The pinned proof takes a compact uniform upper bound D′≥1 for the real determinant and divides by it. The exposition additionally evaluates that Jacobian by singular values. This calculation provides an admissible exact multiplier; the cited formal proof only needs its compact bound.",
      "dependencies": [],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-unfolding-real-jacobian"
      ],
