    {
      "id": "CUD-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-compact-unfolding-bound",
      "title": "From ambient volume to a compact integral of the moving frame",
      "statement": "For continuous centrally invariant real q-forms on the positive cone there is a fixed compact K′ in the special linear group such that ∫_K ‖ω‖dμ ≤ C₂∫_(K′) ‖fr ω‖dν. One may take R′=3NR/2, B=(N²R′²)^q and C₂=D₀ B μ(K₁)/ν(W).",
      "hypotheses": "The ambient space has the maximum entry norm and additive Haar measure μ. The group measure ν is left and right Haar; the arithmetic application comes with such a measure. The finite rank N, degree q, compact K and measures are held fixed before the form is chosen.",
      "correspondence": "The pointwise bound uses the entries of X=sY to bound the inverse tangent map by N²R′². Scalar invariance removes c from the frame, and right translation sends W to WT⊆K′. The source swaps two finite restricted integrals and then chooses a representative only for fixed p. Its compact unfolding hypothesis is supplied to the simplex estimate before the separate arithmetic overlap argument.",
      "dependencies": [
        "CUD-01",
        "CUD-02"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-compact-unfolding-constant"
      ],
